rred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2023-09-04T15:31:04Z","label":{"name":"area: Routing","color":"1830A5"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1707799287","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/54984#issuecomment-1707799287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/54984","id":1707799287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBC3Cis5lyvL3","user":{"login":"wiiiimm","id":179761,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTc2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179761?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm","html_url":"https://github.com/wiiiimm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiiiimm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-06T07:15:31Z","updated_at":"2023-09-06T07:15:31Z","body":"@blauakqa I think `trailingSlash` and `skipTrailingSlashRedirect` are working as intended and they have just been a little misunderstood.\r\n\r\n## `trailingSlash` \r\n\r\n> By default Next.js will redirect urls with trailing slashes to their counterpart without a trailing slash. For example /about/ will redirect to /about. You can configure this behavior to act the opposite way, where urls without trailing slashes are redirected to their counterparts with trailing slashes.\r\n\r\nWhen enabled:\r\n1. `<Link href=\"/about\">About</Link>` will take visitors to `/about/`\r\n2. Request to `/about` will get redirected to `/about/`\r\n\r\nWhen disabled:\r\n1. `<Link href=\"/about\">About</Link>` will take visitors to `/about`\r\n2. Request to `/about/` will get redirected to `/about`\r\n\r\n## With `skipTrailingSlashRedirect` set to true, the redirects mentioned in point 2 above will not occur:\r\n1. Request to `/about/` will render the about page under `/about/`\r\n2. Request to `/about` will render the about page under `/about`\r\n\r\n\r\n## Demo\r\n\r\nI forked your repo, tested with Next.js 13.4.19 and canary (v13.4.20-canary.18) and everything seems fine.\r\n\r\nThis is what I get running on my local:\r\nhttp://localhost:3000/link-with-slash/\r\n![CleanShot 2023-09-06 at 14 33 57](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/assets/179761/5fea95a4-3efb-44e7-b9e5-4335e0899632)\r\nhttp://localhost:3000/link-with-slash\r\n![CleanShot 2023-09-06 at 15 10 45](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/assets/179761/285740bd-9d40-44a1-9f29-bf33cffa42fd)\r\n\r\n\r\ndeployed v13.4.19:\r\nhttps://154699-nextjs-trailing-slash-issue-git-13-4-9.preview.vercel-support.app/link-with-slash/\r\n![CleanShot 2023-09-06 at 15 14 38](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/assets/179761/1e5d5243-005d-4732-8dee-7d6a48666bff)\r\nhttps://154699-nextjs-trailing-slash-issue-git-13-4-9.preview.vercel-support.app/link-with-slash\r\n![CleanShot 2023-09-06 at 15 14 53](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/assets/179761/22cab61c-1b3b-4145-853f-935ae2def44c)\r\n","